Frontmatter is read as YAML, by the YAML engine's rules: a value written over several lines (a
quoted or plain scalar continued on the next line, or a `|` or `>` block) prints its first
paragraph on one line, its lines joined by spaces, as a JSON string; a key holding a list or a
mapping prints alone, as in a YAML file's outline. File mode prints every field uncut, as it
prints a header comment's whole first paragraph.
== args
input/agent.md
== file input/agent.md
---
description: "Starts here and
  continues here"
plain: first part
  second part
block: >-
  folded text
literal: |
  Use this agent when code changed.

  Examples follow.
tags:
  - a
count: 3
---
# Agent
== stdout
input/agent.md (16 lines)
description: "Starts here and continues here"
plain: "first part second part"
block: "folded text"
literal: "Use this agent when code changed."
tags
count: 3
[L16-L16] # Agent
== stderr
== exit 0
